# SPRINT-NNN — Execution Log

> Append-only companion to [`../SPRINT-NNN-<slug>.md`](../SPRINT-NNN-<slug>.md). Uncapped by design:
> this file grows with the work done, which is exactly why it is not inside the Plan's 400-line
> budget (STANDARD §9 · ADR-014). **Never edit a past entry** — correct it with a new one.
>
> The Plan is frozen at promote. A mid-sprint pivot that shifts scope is logged here as a
> `scope-change` entry — what broke · impact · re-confirm G2 — **before** § Plan is edited.

<!-- Newest entries at the BOTTOM: this reads as a chronology, unlike CHANGELOG.md which is
     newest-first. Event is one of: promote · progress · surprise · scope-change · park · blocker ·
     run-complete · close · handoff. `run-complete` is reserved for the run itself finishing (carries
     the Part 4 rollup) — a task finishing mid-run is logged as `progress`, never as `complete`. -->

### YYYY-MM-DD | [event] | [one-line summary]
[detail — what changed and why it matters. Name the task (Tn) it belongs to.]

<!-- A `handoff` entry is the repo-side status stub STANDARD §12(b) prescribes (SPRINT-094 T2):
     `/handoff` writes one at `live`; a later `handoff` entry sharing the SAME handoff-path updates
     it (`consumed` when a session resumes and continues; `spent` when close reconciles it) — the
     LATEST entry per path is authoritative, never edited in place. Both fields are required; either
     missing reads as UNKNOWN, which a sprint may never close over. No sprint to log into (governance
     work, `/triage`, a research session)? The same two-field shape goes in root `HANDOFF-LEDGER.md`
     instead (create-lazily), checked by scripts/lib/check-handoff-state.sh. -->
### YYYY-MM-DD | handoff | [one-line focus of the temp-dir doc]
handoff-status: live | consumed | spent
handoff-path: [absolute temp path /handoff printed]

